      <h2>Part 2: NCP Procedural Analysis</h2>
      <hr>

      <h3>Parent code 10: Host Country (Where the Harm Occurred)</h3>
      <p>This category indicates the geographical location where the harm or human rights violations took place.</p>

      <h3>Parent code 11: Analysis of Context of the NCP Statements</h3>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <h4>11.1 Analysis of Context of the NCP Statements >> Determination of compliance/non-compliance</h4>
          <p>This code analyses when the NCP determines whether the enterprise has complied with its responsibilities under the OECD Guidelines.</p>
        </li>

        <li>
          <h4>11.2 Analysis of Context of the NCP Statements >> Reference/Analysis of Relevant Laws/Regulations</h4>
          <p>This code is about whether the NCP has used or referred to international laws, instruments, legal principles, or policies in its reasoning.</p>
        </li>

        <li>
          <h4>11.3 Analysis of Context of the NCP Statements >> Reference to Previous Similar NCP Statements</h4>
          <p>This code is about when NCPs refer to other previous NCP statements in their case analysis.</p>
        </li>

        <li>
          <h4>11.4 Analysis of Context of the NCP Statements >> Explanation of OECD Guidelines on Certain Matters</h4>
          <p>This code is about how NCPs analyse the applicability of the OECD Guidelines on certain matters. It also covers how the NCP determines whether different versions of the OECD Guidelines, such as those from 2000, 2011, and 2023, apply in certain cases.</p>
      </ul>

      <h3>Parent code 12: Challenges in NCP Proceeding</h3>
      <p>This category is about challenges that prevent the NCP from effectively resolving the case, such as delays, parallel procedures, breach of confidentiality requirements, etc.</p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <h4>12.1 Challenges in NCP Proceeding >> Difficulty in Verification/Validation of Evidence/Link</h4>
          <p>This code is about the challenges in verifying the authenticity and relevance of evidence in NCP proceedings to determine whether the issue is substantiated and establish a link between harm and corporate involvement.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h4>12.2 Challenges in NCP Proceeding >> Issues with Parallel Proceedings</h4>
          <p>This code is about the complications arising from parallel legal or administrative proceedings in NCP cases.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h4>12.3 Challenges in NCP Proceeding >> Delays</h4>
          <p>This code is about the various factors that can cause significant delays in NCP proceedings.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h4>12.4 Challenges in NCP Proceeding >> Challenges regarding NCP mandate/role</h4>
          <p>This code is about the ambiguities and disputes related to the NCP's mandate and role.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h4>12.5 Challenges in NCP Proceeding >> Issues with Confidentiality</h4>
          <p>This code is about the difficulties in maintaining confidentiality in NCP proceedings, the potential for breaches, and how it affects trust between the parties.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h4>12.6 Challenges in NCP Proceeding >> Challenges for individual complainants</h4>
          <p>This code is about the challenges for individual complainants in NCP proceedings.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h4>12.7 Challenges in NCP Proceeding >> Other Challenges</h4>
          <p>This code is about other challenges in NCP proceedings.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h4>12.8 Challenges in NCP Proceeding >> Language barriers</h4>
          <p>This code is about the language differences that can impede effective communication and understanding in NCP proceedings.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h4>12.9 Challenges in NCP Proceeding >> Burden of Costs (Travel, translation, Expert Fees)</h4>
          <p>This code is about the high costs associated with travel, translation, and expert fees that can be a burden in NCP proceedings.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Parent code 13: NCPs Investigation and Mediation Approaches</h3>
      <p>This category covers the various methods and strategies employed by NCPs during their investigation and mediation processes to effectively resolve the case.</p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <h4>13.1 NCPs Investigation and Mediation Approaches >> Approaches/Penalties for Corporate Non-Participation</h4>
          <p>This is about how NCPs seek to involve businesses in their mediation processes and the penalties for non-participation.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h4>13.2 NCPs Investigation and Mediation Approaches >> Effective Cooperation Between NCPs</h4>
          <p>This code is about the effectiveness of the cooperation and coordination between different NCPs during investigations and the mediation process, including both effective and ineffective cooperation.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h4>13.3 NCPs Investigation and Mediation Approaches >> Field Investigation</h4>
          <p>This code is about conducting on-site investigations to gather information and evidence.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h4>13.4 NCPs Investigation and Mediation Approaches >> Hired Legal Experts/Consultants</h4>
          <p>This code is about the involvement of legal experts or consultancy to aid in the investigation or mediation process.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h4>13.5 NCPs Investigation and Mediation Approaches >> Hired Professional Mediators</h4>
          <p>This code is about the involvement of professional mediators to aid in the investigation or mediation process.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h4>13.6 NCPs Investigation and Mediation Approaches >> Legal Advice</h4>
          <p>This code is about the legal advice provided by NCPs during investigations and the mediation process.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h4>13.7 NCPs Investigation and Mediation Approaches >> Other</h4>
          <p>This code is about other approaches and strategies employed by NCPs during investigations and the mediation process.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h4>13.8 NCPs Investigation and Mediation Approaches >> Reporting</h4>
          <p>This code is about the reporting of adverse impacts on human rights and the environment.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h4>13.9 NCPs Investigation and Mediation Approaches >> Communication about Adverse Impacts</h4>
          <p>This code is about the communication of adverse impacts on human rights and the environment.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>
        Parent code 14: Outcome/Result of the NCP Case
      </h3>

      <p>This parent code captures the various possible outcomes and results of cases handled by National Contact Points (NCPs). It includes a range of resolutions, agreements, and actions that may arise from the NCP process, highlighting the effectiveness and impact of NCP interventions. The outcomes may include formal agreements, cessation of harmful activities, policy changes, acknowledgments, financial compensation, and other forms of resolution. Each sub-code under this parent code provides specific insights into the types of results that can emerge from the NCP's mediation and investigative efforts.</p>


      <ul>
        <li>
          <h4>14.1 Outcome/Result of the NCP Case >> Agreement Outside the NCP Proceeding</h4>
          <p>This code is about cases where an agreement was reached outside the formal NCP proceedings.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h4>14.2 Outcome/Result of the NCP Case >> Cease of Activity/Disengagement</h4>
          <p>This code is about cases where the company ceased certain activities as a result of the NCP proceedings and also about the cases where the company disengaged from certain business activities or suppliers following the NCP proceedings.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h4>14.3 Outcome/Result of the NCP Case >> No Agreement</h4>
          <p>This code is about cases where no agreement was reached during the NCP proceedings.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h4>14.4 Outcome/Result of the NCP Case >> Acknowledgements/Apologies</h4>
          <p>This code is about cases where the company issued acknowledgements or apologies as a result of the NCP proceedings.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h4>14.5 Outcome/Result of the NCP Case >> Changes of Actions/Policy Made by the Result of NCP Proceedings</h4>
          <p>This code is about policy or action changes in company management as a result of NCP proceedings.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h4>14.6 Outcome/Result of the NCP Case >> Written Agreement Resulted by the NCP Proceeding</h4>
          <p>This code is about cases where a written agreement, memorandum, mandate, or other contract was concluded at the end of the NCP procedure.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h4>14.7 Outcome/Result of the NCP Case >> Financial Compensation/Refund</h4>
          <p>This code is about cases where financial compensation was provided as a result of the NCP proceedings.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>

